WEBVTT

00:00.199 --> 00:02.440
Skilled people stuck pressing the

00:02.440 --> 00:04.759
same buttons all day

00:04.759 --> 00:06.160
because that's the only way the

00:06.160 --> 00:07.320
machine listens.

00:07.965 --> 00:10.525
We gave machines with no API a

00:10.525 --> 00:13.405
way to talk to Meta's models.

00:13.405 --> 00:16.085
This is Physical MCP.

00:16.085 --> 00:19.205
Four layers, one button press,

00:19.205 --> 00:21.684
a webcam, two tiny servos, and a

00:21.684 --> 00:23.845
small board pointed at a machine.

00:25.059 --> 00:25.699
The eyes.

00:26.099 --> 00:28.539
SAM 3.1 finds every button

00:28.539 --> 00:29.619
and reads the screen.

00:30.219 --> 00:32.019
If it can't read it, it stops.

00:32.419 --> 00:33.929
It never presses blind.

00:35.059 --> 00:37.339
The brain. Muse Spark turns a

00:37.339 --> 00:39.339
plain request into a plan of

00:39.339 --> 00:40.618
presses.

00:40.618 --> 00:41.899
And if a job isn't safe or

00:41.899 --> 00:44.099
possible, it says no.

00:45.058 --> 00:45.978
The gut check.

00:46.498 --> 00:48.738
Before anything risky, Muse Spark Open

00:48.738 --> 00:50.858
scores the risk and explains why.

00:51.218 --> 00:52.978
Then a human makes the call.

00:53.518 --> 00:54.358
The fingers,

00:54.638 --> 00:56.318
two three-dollar servos.

00:56.718 --> 00:58.987
The AI never sees them.

00:59.522 --> 01:00.923
Do you want to see it live?

01:01.497 --> 01:03.376
Here's Physical MCP watching a

01:03.376 --> 01:04.816
kitchen timer.

01:04.816 --> 01:06.776
We ask it to set T1 to two

01:06.776 --> 01:08.696
hours and start it.

01:08.696 --> 01:10.096
Muse Spark reads the screen and

01:10.096 --> 01:12.936
plans three presses. H, H, then

01:12.936 --> 01:13.817
start.

01:14.492 --> 01:15.931
While the finger gets to work,

01:15.931 --> 01:17.892
Muse Spark Open scores the plan

01:17.892 --> 01:19.892
in the background. It flags step

01:19.892 --> 01:22.532
three as medium risk. The first

01:22.532 --> 01:24.891
two presses just add hours, so

01:24.891 --> 01:26.612
they run on their own. After each

01:26.612 --> 01:28.492
one, the camera checks the screen.

01:28.492 --> 01:30.852
But starting the timer is a real

01:30.852 --> 01:32.652
action. So it stops and asks a

01:32.652 --> 01:34.972
human with the reason right there.

01:34.972 --> 01:36.572
Hold for one and a half seconds

01:36.572 --> 01:37.852
to approve

01:37.852 --> 01:39.652
and it's running. Job done.

01:40.885 --> 01:42.965
Same brain, different machine. This

01:42.965 --> 01:45.125
one's a simulated incubator.

01:45.125 --> 01:46.925
We just ask set it to 37 and

01:46.925 --> 01:48.525
run it for 2 hours.

01:48.525 --> 01:50.404
Muse Spark is planning.

01:50.404 --> 01:51.604
Muse Spark has never seen this

01:51.604 --> 01:52.845
panel. It plans from what the

01:52.845 --> 01:54.285
camera finds.

01:54.285 --> 01:56.125
Six presses. After each one it

01:56.125 --> 01:57.765
reads the screen and only moves

01:57.765 --> 02:00.004
on once the number matches.

02:00.004 --> 02:01.485
Starting heat is risky, so it

02:01.485 --> 02:04.084
stops. Spark Open says why and I

02:04.084 --> 02:05.845
hold to approve.

02:05.845 --> 02:08.885
Succeeded. All six steps verified.

02:08.885 --> 02:10.365
All six verified

02:10.365 --> 02:11.965
and every press, every check

02:11.965 --> 02:13.845
and every approval is locked.

02:14.857 --> 02:16.457
Replacing a lab machine cost about

02:16.457 --> 02:18.776
$1,000, retrofitting it 2 to

02:18.776 --> 02:21.736
20,000. We did it with about $20

02:21.736 --> 02:25.456
in parts and 14 cents per job. 6

02:25.456 --> 02:27.937
out of 7 full jobs worked.

02:27.937 --> 02:29.977
50 for 50 on the bench. Same

02:29.977 --> 02:32.217
start button, medium risk at 37

02:32.217 --> 02:34.337
degrees, high at 90.

02:34.337 --> 02:36.176
Here's the stack we used to build

02:36.176 --> 02:37.657
and we used Muse Code to build a

02:37.657 --> 02:39.977
website. Next, onboard any

02:39.977 --> 02:42.096
machine from one photo. Run fleets

02:42.096 --> 02:44.977
remotely. Add a hardware e-stop.

02:44.977 --> 02:46.416
Labs first,

02:46.416 --> 02:48.536
then factories, kitchens, and

02:48.536 --> 02:49.536
anyone who can't reach small

02:49.536 --> 02:50.217
buttons.

02:50.498 --> 02:52.098
built by Bhavisha and Pam.

02:52.458 --> 02:54.378
Give your machines an API.
